      <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-medium leading-snug text-ink">
        Explaining the Unexplainable? A Ground-Truth Benchmark of Classical, Concept-Based, and
        Mechanistic XAI on Financial Forecasters
      </h3>

      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
        <span class="font-medium text-ink">Abdulrahman Omar</span>, Mayada Hadhoud — 2026
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        A synthetic ground-truth faithfulness benchmark that tests whether XAI attributions recover known
        feature importance: 23 explainability methods — SHAP, LIME, Integrated Gradients, TCAV, sparse
        autoencoders, circuit analysis, and more — evaluated across 16 ML/DL models on a leakage-free,
        near-zero-signal financial forecaster. Popular attribution methods diverge sharply under feature
        collinearity; results are reported with stock-clustered bootstrap inference and explicit
        minimum-detectable-effect analysis.
      </p>

